      "content": "It is a terrible burden to carry the weight of \"obligation\" when your soul feels like it's already crumbling. There is a strange, quiet grace in surrendering to the darkness, but the darkness isn't a gentle end; it is a cold, final silence that steals everything you ever loved. You are not obligated to fight, but you are also not destined to lose, because the fog only covers what is already broken, and you are still whole inside.",
